1
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:06,450
走吧 伙计 该上学了
Let's go, buddy. Schooltime.

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,440
歌洛莉亚 如果你待会和你闺蜜有约
Oh, and Gloria, if you want to get together with the girls later,

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,900
我可以自己看看橄榄球赛什么的
I could just, you know, watch the football game or something.

4
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,120
其实他就是想看橄榄球赛
That means he wants to watch a football game.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,540
我不是和你说话
I'm not talking to you.

6
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,420
你为什么要喝咖啡
What are you drinking coffee for anyway?

7
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,660
这是我的文化习俗 我是哥伦比亚人
It's my culture. I'm Colombian.

8
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,740
是吗 这些法式吐司
Oh, yeah? What part of Colombia

9
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,460
也是哥伦比亚的吗
are those French toaster sticks from?

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,297
亲爱的 我不太确定你今天能看比赛
Babe, I'm not sure about the game.

11
00:00:26,297 --> 00:00:28,952
因为全家人都要过来烧烤
The whole family's coming over for the barbecue.

12
00:00:28,952 --> 00:00:30,634
-是今天吗 -没错
- That's today? - See.

13
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,340
今天可是俄亥俄州赛
It's the Ohio State game.

14
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,160
那又怎样 每个人都能看
So? Everybody can watch.

15
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,940
我不喜欢和不懂球的人一起看比赛
I don't like watching the game with people who don't know the game.

16
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:37,739
七嘴八舌乱指点
People talk.

17
00:00:37,739 --> 00:00:39,400
你也会乱指点我的橄榄球比赛
You talk at my football games.

18
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,620
首先 你那个是足球
For one thing, it's called soccer.

19
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,920
而且你们队整个赛季只得了两分
Your team scored two goals all season.

20
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,220
我随便说也不会冒风险
I'm not taking a big risk.

21
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,440
你到底喝了多少啊
How much of this did you drink?

22
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:50,540
饶了我吧 我今天得去攀绳呢
Give me a break. I have to climb a rope today.

23
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,240
-妈妈 -怎么了
- Hey, Mom. - Yeah?

24
00:00:55,101 --> 00:00:57,430
能给我40块钱吃午饭吗
Can I have $40 for lunch?

25
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:58,700
40块
Forty dollars?

26
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,495
-学校还让我们买本书 -什么书
- I also need a book for school. - What book?

27
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:03,840
我想买条裙子
I want a dress.

28
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:06,920
你知道你撒谎撒得多失败吗
Do you have any idea what a bad liar you are?

29
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:08,417
我更担心的是
I'd be more worried that

30
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:10,474
她连一本书的名字都想不出来
she couldn't come up with a single book title.

31
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,260
卢克 快点 我们要迟到了
Luke, come on. We're late.

32
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:16,380
这是第一次里外前后全都穿反了
Mmm, there's a first- inside out and backwards.

33
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:17,759
至少他没把衣服塞进...
At least it isn't zipped into his...

34
00:01:17,759 --> 00:01:19,754
好吧 真塞进去了
Oh. There it is.

35
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:23,060
有人是"读书大智慧" 也有人是"市井小聪明"
Well, there's book smart, and then there's street smart.

36
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:24,360
没错 卢克属于第三类怪胎
Yeah, and then there's Luke.

37
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:27,305
他只是 他只是好奇心重 仅此而已
Oh, he's just... He's just curious. That's all.

38
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:30,960
他有着科学家的头脑
He's got this almost scientific mind...

39
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,460
以及对知识的渴望
with a thirst for knowledge.

40
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:36,420
他像小爱因斯坦一样
He's like this little Einstein.

41
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,280
有些人会问"为什么"
Some people ask, "Why?"

42
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:42,380
但卢克会问"为什么不呢"
Luke asks, "Why not?"

43
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,940
我经常问"为什么"
I ask "Why?" a lot.

44
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:50,220
我们在十码区 现在是五码区
We're at the ten. We're at the five.

45
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,880
到达一码 爸爸 我们触地得分啦
We're at the one. Daddy, we're scoring a touchdown!

46
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,661
别 小心别弄伤孩子了
No, please... please don't spike our baby.

47
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,640
为什么她穿得像汉堡神偷公仔
Why is she dressed like the Hamburglar?

48
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:58,800
她是裁判
She's a referee.

49
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,760
我们今晚一定要去我爸那里吗
Do... Do we even have to go to my dad's tonight?

50
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,100
你在开玩笑吗 今晚是俄亥俄州赛
Are you kidding me? We're playing Ohio State.

51
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,880
我收集古董钢笔
I collect antique fountain pens.

52
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,400
我很擅长日式插花技术
I'm quite adept at Japanese flower arrangement-

53
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:09,600
"花道"
ikebana-

54
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:13,080
而且我曾是伊利诺伊大学的首发进攻内锋
and I was a starting offensive lineman at the University of Illinois.

55
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:14,720
惊讶吧
Surprise.

56
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:17,320
-我不喜欢橄榄球 -你知道吗
- I don't like football. - You know what?

57
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,119
我认为维持恋情的一方面
I thought part of being in a relationship...

58
00:02:19,119 --> 00:02:21,016
就是要爱屋及乌
was pretending to enjoy your partner's interests.

59
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:24,256
你以为我真的喜欢做腌菜吗
Do you think I really loved home pickle-making?

60
00:02:24,256 --> 00:02:25,660
是的 因为你确实喜欢
Yeah, 'cause you did.

61
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,360
就喜欢一周
For a week,

62
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,600
到后来别人都以为我们是到处送腌菜的怪胎
until we became the weird guys who gave everybody pickles.

63
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,680
马文 谢谢邀请我们到你温馨的家来
Oh, thank you, Marvin, for inviting us into your lovely home.

64
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,404
给你 请收下这包腌菜
Here. Would you care for a sack of pickles?

65
00:02:33,404 --> 00:02:34,740
你真可爱
It was charming.

66
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,940
我们是腌菜工 米奇尔
We were picklers, Mitchell.

67
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,800
好吧 那就算了
Okay, you know what? Fine.

68
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,500
和你的小剪刀待在家里吧
Stay home with your little jagged scissors.

69
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,120
你可以继续弄你的剪贴簿
Maybe catch up on your scrapbooking.

70
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,460
拜托 你也喜欢剪贴簿啊
Come... You loved scrapbooking.

71
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:45,440
我有吗 米奇尔 我有吗
Did I, Mitchell? Did I?

72
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:48,060
够了 别以为搞个双重反问就是真的了
Stop. Don't do the "Double question to prove a point" thing.

73
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,360
我讨厌别人那么做
I hate it when people do that.

74
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,460
是吗 米奇尔 是吗
Do you, Mitchell? Do you?

75
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:52,540
别闹了 莉莉
Stop, Lily.

76
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,160
没问题 我们马上过来 谢谢
No problem. We'll be right down. Thanks.

77
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:17,420
亲爱的 怎么了
Hey, honey. What's up?

78
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,880
学校刚刚来电话了 卢克打架了
The school just called. Luke got in a fight.

79
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:22,840
天呐 他还好吗
Oh, geez. Is he okay?

80
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:25,700
他没事 但老师想要我们去一趟
Yeah, he's fine, but they want us to come down there.

81
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,880
-你在哪里 -我在带人看房子
- Where are you? - I'm showing a house.

82
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,240
什么房子
What house?

83
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,840
我在打高尔夫球
I'm golfing.

84
00:03:37,743 --> 00:03:39,220
我猜是那个叫德卡斯的小孩
I bet it was that Durkas kid.

85
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:40,103
我讨厌那个小孩
I hate that kid.

86
00:03:40,103 --> 00:03:41,100
也许是他突然挑衅卢克
He probably jumped on Luke

87
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,497
而卢克只是反抗而已
and Luke just fought back.

88
00:03:42,497 --> 00:03:45,400
-那小孩真讨厌 -他曾经取笑我的头发
- Kid's a menace. - He made fun of my hair once.

89
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,800
嘘 他的家长可能在里面
Shh. The parents are probably in there.

90
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,200
我只是睡觉把头发睡乱了
I slept on it funny.

91
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,360
就好像他没有过一样
Like that never happened to him?

92
00:03:49,895 --> 00:03:50,868
走吧
Come on.

93
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,780
你们在这里干嘛
What are you doing here?

94
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,980
这两个笨蛋在一起打架
These two knuckleheads were fighting each other.

95
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:58,081
-什么 -幸好是你啊
- What? - Could've been worse.

96
00:03:58,352 --> 00:04:01,022
我还没准备好今天面对德卡斯
I was not ready to face Durkas today.

97
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,579
发生什么事了
So what happened?

98
00:04:02,579 --> 00:04:05,040
很明显 在操场上发生了骂人
Well, apparently there was some name-calling

99
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,320
和斗殴的事情
and shoving on the playground.

100
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,260
老师把他们分开的时候
By the time a teacher separated them,

101
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:10,360
卢克正坐在曼尼的胸上
Luke was sitting on Manny's chest.

102
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,380
-卢克 那可不像你啊 -等等
- Luke, that's not like you. - Wait a minute.

103
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,380
-你是卢克的爸爸吗 -外公
- You're Luke's father? - Grandfather.

104
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:17,560
-那么曼尼的爸爸是 -哈维尔
- So Manny's father is... - Javier.

105
00:04:17,643 --> 00:04:20,752
一个疯子 就是从他身上遗传到的暴脾气
Crazy guy. That's where he gets his fire.

106
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,900
-好吧 你是 -他是我们的儿子
- Okay, you're... - He's our son.

107
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:24,920
-我的外孙 -我是他女儿
- And my grandson. - I'm his daughter.

108
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:26,800
-那么你是 -他小舅舅
- So you're... - His uncle.

109
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,100
你要再敢这么说 我还会坐到你的胸上
Stop saying that or I'll sit on your chest again.

110
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,260
等一下 打架就是因为这个吗
Ho! Wait a second. Is that what this was all about?

111
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,780
他一直说我是他的外甥
He keeps calling me his nephew.

112
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:34,820
你就是我的外甥
You are my nephew.

113
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,240
-闭嘴 -好了 好了
- Shut up! - Okay, okay.

114
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,920
我明白了 你们似乎是一家人
I'm getting the sense that you're all related, uh, somehow.

115
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,340
所以 也许你们最好能回家自己解决
So it's probably best if you work this out at home...

116
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,120
这样孩子们就能回去上课了 好吗
so the boys can go back to class, okay?

117
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,560
但是我们很生气你们这样 小伙子们
But we're not happy about this, boys.

118
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,200
这不是成熟的年轻小伙的行为
This is not how mature young men behave.

119
00:04:49,438 --> 00:04:51,081
把这便条给"帕斯沃"老师
Here's your note for Miss Passwater.

120
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
我并不担心 他们都是好孩子
Look, I wouldn't worry. They're good kids.

121
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,340
只是当某个孩子比较怪异时 会有点难处理
It's just tough when one kid's a little different.

122
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,360
-是的 -是的
- Yes. - Yes.

123
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,000
你听到她那么说了 对吗
You heard how she said that, right?

124
00:05:05,719 --> 00:05:07,013
"是的"
"Yes."

125
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,580
她觉得卢克是怪异的那个 卢克
She thought Luke was the weird one. Luke.

126
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,440
她家孩子把自己的头卡在家具里
Her kid gets his head stuck in the furniture,

127
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,240
还好意思说曼尼怪异
and Manny is the different one.

128
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,240
我来告诉你什么怪异
I will tell you what's weird.

129
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,080
我们的孩子并不怪异
Our son is not weird.

130
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,020
怪异的是她的孩子抹须后水
What's weird is that her kid wears aftershave

131
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,100
而且打扮得像个伯爵
and dresses like a count.

132
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,280
我想我们别请他们过来烧烤了
I think we should cancel with them for the barbecue.

133
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,420
如果我们不去 只会把问题越闹越大
If we cancel, it'll just make this a bigger deal than it is.

134
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:27,280
让卢克和曼尼多相处一下对他们两个都好
It'll be good for Luke and Manny to spend some time.

135
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,720
-也许对你和歌洛莉亚也好 -为什么
- Might be good for you and Gloria too. - Why?

136
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,740
她一直对我有意见
She's always had a problem with me.

137
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,920
我觉得我该找出是什么问题
I think I'm gonna find out what it is.

138
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:37,360
那是你最不该做的
That's the worst thing you could do.

139
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,720
就当没发生过 忍忍就过去了
Just sweep it under the rug.

140
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,400
-我可不是个"忍者" -听我的没错
- I'm not a sweeper. - Trust me on this.

141
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:43,140
我觉得你们俩得谈谈这件事
I think you two need to talk it out.

142
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,320
我跟她没什么好说的
I don't have anything to say to her.

143
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,140
她才是有问题的那个 不是我
She's the one with the problem, not me.

144
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,440
你到底向着谁
Whose side are you on?

145
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,700
她是我的女儿 你是我的妻子
She's my daughter. You're my wife.

146
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:53,400
让我们先理清重点
Let's remember what's important here.

147
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,840
橄榄球赛马上就开始了
There's a football game on.

148
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:57,780
我只是不想我的两个女孩相处得不好
I just hate it when my two girls aren't getting along.

149
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,140
她怎么成你的女孩了
How exactly is she your girl?

150
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:08,700
我为聚会准备了一点东西
I got a few things for the party.

151
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:09,700
莉莉准备好要走了吗
Is Lily ready to go?

152
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:12,180
是的 她准备好了
Oh, yeah, yeah. She's ready.

153
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:13,920
怎么了
What's wrong?

154
00:06:14,181 --> 00:06:17,580
我真的很担心C·J·海托
I'm just really worried about C.J. Hightower.

155
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:18,400
他脚踝受伤了
With the bad ankle,

156
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,440
我不知道他要怎么跑完三角线路
I don't know how he's gonna run his corner routes.

157
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,760
我男友刚刚说了什么呀
What did my boyfriend just say?

158
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:26,220
我听了你之前说的 我同意你的话
Listen, I heard what you said, and I thought, yes,

159
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,380
我应该多了解一下橄榄球
I should try to learn more about football.

160
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,640
你这么做真是成熟了
That is very mature of you.

161
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:33,000
我觉得 橄榄球迷都能学会
I figure, if football fans can learn it,

162
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,080
那能有多难呢
how hard can it be?

163
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,560
就你最聪明
That's very elitist of you.

164
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,000
我才刚刚起步 好不
I'm taking baby steps here, all right?

165
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:40,220
其实 我真的很期待
I'm actually- I'm really looking forward to it.

166
00:06:40,302 --> 00:06:41,661
因为这不仅仅是比赛
'Cause it's not just the game.

167
00:06:41,661 --> 00:06:45,860
而且现场彩旗招展 锣鼓喧天
It's-It's the bands and the drama, the pageantry.

168
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,511
别忘了还有球队的吉祥物
Don't forget about the team mascots.

169
00:06:47,511 --> 00:06:48,640
他们戴"宽领带"吗
They wear ascots?

170
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,540
不是 是"吉祥物" 有个"M"开头
No. Mascots. With an "M."

171
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,260
要是在外人面前你就丢脸了
That could have been very embarrassing.

172
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:53,800
好吧
Okay.

173
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:55,420
直吗
Am I straight?

174
00:06:57,763 --> 00:07:00,768
我也不知道你是直男还是什么
I'm not sure what you are right now.

175
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:03,472
你们好吗
How ya doin'?

176
00:07:03,472 --> 00:07:05,035
-外公好 -小美女好
- Hey, Gramps. - Hi, beautiful.

177
00:07:05,035 --> 00:07:06,677
你好 菲尔 见到你真好
Hi, Phil. Good to see ya.

178
00:07:06,677 --> 00:07:08,260
让我猜猜 比赛开始了吗
Let me guess. Game's on?

179
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,040
刚开始
Just started.

180
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,800
送给你的
Hey. For you.

181
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,380
很高兴见到你 歌洛莉亚
It's nice to see you, Gloria.

182
00:07:13,741 --> 00:07:15,159
今天两次哦
Ah! Two times today.

183
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:17,143
-抱两次好啊 -菲尔
- Okay, well... - Uh, Phil?

184
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,520
她的意思是我们今天见了两次
She means we've seen them two times today.

185
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:22,360
大家听着 吃的在那边 喝的在那边
Okay, everybody, the food's in there. The drinks are in there.

186
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,180
-我进屋去了 -等等 杰
- I'll be in here. - Hold on, Jay.

187
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:27,220
我觉得我们不该忽视明显存在的一个问题
I think we should address the elephant in the room.

188
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:30,504
卢克 曼尼 都过来
Uh, Luke, Manny. Bring it in.

189
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,600
快点 聚在一起
Come on. Huddle up.

190
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:34,140
像打橄榄球一样
Football.

191
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:38,040
鉴于今天在学校里发生的事情
Now in light of what happened at school today,

192
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,720
你们有什么想说的吗
do you have any feelings you'd like to express?

193
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:42,380
我觉得现在是个合适的表达机会
I think this is the proper forum...

194
00:07:42,446 --> 00:07:45,044
老天啊 得了吧 你们两个
For god's sakes. All right, both of you.

195
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:48,420
在这个家里 我们是欺负彼此
Now, in this family, do we kick and punch each other,

196
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,500
还是关爱彼此
or do we love each other?

197
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,360
关爱彼此 这就对了
Love each other. That's right.

198
00:07:51,597 --> 00:07:53,946
我进屋去了
I'II be in the den.

199
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,740
我带了些甜点
So, I brought dessert.

200
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,260
好的 谢谢你
Okay. Thank you.

201
00:08:01,322 --> 00:08:03,828
我也做了派
I make pie too.

202
00:08:04,866 --> 00:08:07,012
派再多也不嫌多 对吧
You can never have too many pies, right?

203
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:09,140
行了
Okay, whoa. Whoa.

204
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,720
大家深呼吸
Everybody take a deep breath.

205
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,020
我们面对现实吧
Let's think about getting real.

206
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:13,180
菲尔 别这样
Phil, no.

207
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,420
为什么说"菲尔 别这样"
Why "Phil, no"?

208
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:15,920
菲尔要干嘛
What is Phil doing?

209
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:17,300
我只是想说出来
I'm just gonna say it.

210
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:18,840
你们俩之间的紧张气氛
There's tension between you two.

211
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,960
已经弥漫出来了
Bam. It's out there.

212
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:21,200
我要宰了你
I'm gonna kill you.

213
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:25,001
我想他是对的 而且我们应该谈谈
I think he's right, and I think we should talk about it.

214
00:08:25,001 --> 00:08:27,147
我就是想说这个
That's what I'm talkin' about...

215
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:31,680
你们谈谈 这个事儿
you two talking... about it.

216
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:37,180
我喜欢橄榄球
I like football.

217
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,900
海莉很讨厌 这很奇怪
Haley hates it, which is weird

218
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:42,460
因为里面全是男孩 也不必看书
because it's all boys... and there's no reading required.

219
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,160
你知道吗 她每天早上
Do you know that she spends

220
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,900
至少花45分钟弄她的头发
at least 45 minutes every morning doing her hair?

221
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:48,140
而且有的时候
And then sometimes...

222
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,420
冲啊 伊利诺伊队
Let's go, Illini!

223
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:52,344
冲啊 快冲
Let's go! Right now!

224
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,915
看来我要和迪克·布特库斯一起看比赛了
Looks like I gotta watch the game with Dick Butkus.

225
00:08:54,915 --> 00:08:57,260
老爸 别这样 太冒犯人了
Dad! Dad, come on. That's offensive.

226
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:58,960
米奇尔 那人是伊利诺斯州
Mitchell, he's one of the greatest linebackers

227
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,900
最棒的中后卫球员之一
to ever play at Illinois...

228
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:01,437
也是我自己的偶像之一
and one of my personal heroes.

229
00:09:01,437 --> 00:09:03,342
难道他的名字真是"亲屁股"吗
And his name is "Butt-kiss"?

230
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,460
我们只是想要
We're just choosing to...

231
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,340
好吧 没什么
Okay. All right.

232
00:09:07,787 --> 00:09:09,471
老爸 我以为你恐同呢 抱歉
Dad, I thought you were being homophobic. I'm sorry.

233
00:09:09,471 --> 00:09:11,105
-我们有一整晚要相处呢 -好吧
- We got all night. - Yes, we do.

234
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:13,240
-你要和我们一起看吗 -是的
- Are you joining us here? - Yeah.

235
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,040
杰 你知道吗 他正在钻研呢
Jay, you know what? He's been studying up.

236
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,779
跟你说 我有点担心C·J·海托
I gotta tell ya, I'm a little worried about C.J. Hightower.

237
00:09:17,779 --> 00:09:19,260
没错吧 他脚踝受伤了
Right? With the bad ankle?

238
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,100
我很好奇他怎么能完成三角线路
I'm wondering how he's gonna run his corner routes.

239
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:22,940
-海托不上场 -什么
- Hightower's out. - What?

240
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,957
那谁来跑三角线路
Oh. Then who is gonna run the corner routes?

241
00:09:25,957 --> 00:09:27,983
我来告诉你谁不会上吧 比林斯
I'll tell you who it won't be- Billings.

242
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:30,259
太明显了 他在坐牢
That's low. He's in jail.

243
00:09:30,259 --> 00:09:32,593
是啊 他不会上
Oh, wow. Yeah. Then no.

244
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:33,559
双侧边锋
Double tight end,

245
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:35,352
四分卫要冲到左边了
it's gonna be a quarterback roll-out to the left.

246
00:09:35,352 --> 00:09:36,480
-他们要成功了 -不可能 相信我
- They're gonna run it. - No, trust me.

247
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,100
他抢到位置了
He's got the slot.

248
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:39,355
到达阵区了 触地得分
In the end zone! Touchdown!

249
00:09:39,355 --> 00:09:43,162
真幸运 也许 他们该考虑下闪电战
Lucky call. Maybe they, uh, should've considered blitzing.

250
00:09:43,162 --> 00:09:45,800
闪电战没用的 一边儿凉快去吧
Blitzing wouldn't have helped them. Get outta here.

251
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,640
天呐 闪电战
Oh, gosh. Blitzing.

252
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:52,280
于是 我对橄榄球的兴趣突然消失殆尽
So, my interest in football ended as suddenly and dramatically...

253
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,980
就像《西区故事》在高潮时戛然而止
as the climax of West Side Story.

254
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,380
我是个音乐剧迷
I'm a musical theater fan.

255
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:57,760
惊讶吧
Surprise.

256
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:01,080
好吧 说实话吗
Okay. The truth?

257
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:03,940
有时候我觉得你不喜欢我
I sometimes feel like you don't like me.

258
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,500
开门见山 重磅出击
Powerful, powerful stuff.

259
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,540
克莱尔 告诉我们你怎么想
Claire? Tell us how that makes you feel.

260
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:12,040
此时此刻 我感到怒火中烧啊
Right now, I'm feeling a lot of anger.

261
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,660
别 别跟我说 跟她说
No, don't tell me. Tell her.

262
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,040
歌洛莉亚 我现在很生菲尔的气
Gloria, right now, I'm really angry at Phil.

263
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,800
别跑题了
Let's respect the process.

264
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,840
歌洛莉亚 我不知道
Gloria, I don't know

265
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,260
为什么你觉得我不喜欢你
why you think I don't like you.

266
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,820
有时 你在我面前会摆出那种表情
Sometimes when you see me, you make that face.

267
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,440
什么表情
What face?

268
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,140
就像这样
Like this.

269
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,440
-我才没做过那种表情呢 -我的天啊
- I do not make a face like that. - Oh, my God.

270
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,900
-那可是克莱尔的招牌表情 -米奇尔
- That is so Claire. - Mitchell!

271
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,380
看见没 她对谁都那副表情
See? She does that with everyone.

272
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:34,920
已经习惯成自然了
It's just her face.

273
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,940
不仅仅是那种表情
No, it's not just the face.

274
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,240
从最开始到现在
From the beginning,

275
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,860
我觉得我和曼尼在这个家不受欢迎
I feel like Manny and I are not welcome in this family.

276
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,240
这也太疯狂了吧
That is so crazy.

277
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:45,080
不 一点都不疯狂 是我的真实感受
No, it's not so crazy. It's how I feel.

278
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,500
如果你那么想 我很抱歉
I am sorry if you feel that way.

279
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:54,780
真的很抱歉 从我见到你的那一刻起
I really am, because from the moment I met you,

280
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:58,200
我就想让你融入到我们当中来
I have tried to make you feel comfortable with us.

281
00:10:59,348 --> 00:11:00,860
你觉得这只是我自己胡思乱想
You think it's all in my head?

282
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:02,820
没 有点 我不知道
No. Kind- I don't know.

283
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:06,560
我是说 我们很欢迎你和曼尼加入我们家
I mean, we really love having you and Manny in our family.

284
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:07,560
-真的 -真的
- Really? - Really.

285
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:10,420
所以 你用不着这么有戒心
So, you don't have to be so defensive.

286
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,820
我是有戒心 是吧
I do that, don't I?

287
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,759
有一点吧
Well, a bit.

288
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,000
我觉得应该拥抱了
I'm feeling a hug.

289
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,900
我是想说三人群抱
I was thinking group hug,

290
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:22,820
-但这也不错 -我要能去的话就去了
- But this is nice. - I'd be there if I could.

291
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,240
天啊 这还有人搂搂抱抱呢
Oh, my God. There's hugging.

292
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,180
海莉 不打电话会死啊
Haley, get off the phone already.

293
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:27,300
你去哪了
Where did you go?

294
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:28,554
你听见他说什么了
You heard him.

295
00:11:28,554 --> 00:11:29,760
他说"一边凉快去"
He said, "Get outta here."

296
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,520
天啊 你真像个娇弱的小姑娘
Oh, my God. You're such a girl.

297
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:34,100
爸 反正我也想要喝杯啤酒的
Dad- I was coming to get a beer anyways.

298
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:35,440
你道歉真有诚意
Nice apology.

299
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,120
啤酒真不错
Nice beer.

300
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,360
嘿 两个壮小伙来了
Hey, there are the little roustabouts.

301
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:43,140
-看来你们和好如初了 -没错
- You look like you patched things up pretty good, huh? - Yeah.

302
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,420
我们能从孩子身上学到许多东西啊
Oh, we can learn so much from the children.

303
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,522
现在再回头想想打架的事
Bet it seems kind of silly now

304
00:11:48,522 --> 00:11:49,860
是不是觉得当时很蠢啊
what you were even fighting about, huh?

305
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:52,340
-我笑他的口音 -什么口音
- I made fun of his accent. - What accent?

306
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,840
我笑他每天的午餐都一样
I made fun of him for having the same thing for lunch every day.

307
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:59,560
我取笑他 因为他妈妈以前是挖煤的
I made fun of him because his mom used to dig coal.

308
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:01,320
什么
What?

309
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,600
他说你是个挖煤工
He said you were a coal digger.

310
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,540
好了 我觉得该换个话题了
Okay. I think we can move on.

311
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,500
谁说我是个"挖煤工"
Who said I was a coal digger?

312
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,200
我妈告诉我的
That's what my mom told me.

313
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:10,650
什么是挖煤工
What's a coal digger?

314
00:12:10,650 --> 00:12:11,920
宝贝 他听错了
Sweetheart, he heard it wrong.

315
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,593
那叫"淘金工"[傍大款]
It's "Gold digger."

316
00:12:12,593 --> 00:12:14,520
我得过一会再打给你了
I'm gonna have to call you back.

317
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,779
我真的不记得说过这话
I really do not think that I remember ever saying that.

318
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:19,986
其实 你在车里这么说过
Well, you said in the car.

319
00:12:19,986 --> 00:12:21,556
你圣诞节这么说过
You said it at Christmas.

320
00:12:21,556 --> 00:12:23,301
-你还在墨西哥餐厅这么说过 -好了
- You said it in the Mexican restaurant- - Okay,

321
00:12:23,301 --> 00:12:25,980
乖儿子 你每天丢三落四
Mr. "Leaves His Sweatshirts at School Every Day...

322
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:27,760
今天却记忆如神 真谢谢你了
Suddenly Remembers Everything," Thank you.

323
00:12:29,164 --> 00:12:30,820
还说是我自己胡思乱想 哈
And it was all in my head, huh?

324
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:32,700
听我说 歌洛莉亚 其实
Oh, listen. Gloria, it was...

325
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:35,860
都是一年前的事了 那时我还不了解你呢
like, a year ago, before I knew you.

326
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:36,700
你真行啊
Nice going.

327
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:38,800
搞得我妈和我姐吵架了吧
Now my mom and my sister are fighting.

328
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,860
如果我说了众人都想说的话
If I say something that everybody else is thinking,

329
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,480
是不是意味着我很刻薄呢
does that make me a mean person?

330
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:50,920
或者说我很勇敢呢
Or does it make me a brave person?

331
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,506
我就是一个有勇气
One who is courageous enough to

332
00:12:53,506 --> 00:12:55,550
顶住压力 挺身而出
stand up and-and say something...

333
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,000
在背后悄悄地说
behind someone's back

334
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,127
只敢在小孩面前说
to a 10-year-old.

335
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,620
她现在可是气疯了
Well, she's pissed.

336
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,660
是啊 她甚至连房间都不愿意出了
Yeah. She wouldn't even come out of her room.

337
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:08,780
你真的非要说她是"傍大款的"吗
Did you really have to call her that- a gold digger?

338
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:11,300
知道吗 爸爸 那可是一年前
Well, you know what, Dad? It was a year ago.

339
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:14,060
所以人家自然而然会问啊
And it was a natural question to ask.

340
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:16,320
她那么漂亮 那么性感
She's a beautiful, hot woman,

341
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:20,120
而你却不那么 你懂的
and you're not exactly, you know-

342
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,080
不那么什么
Not exactly what?

343
00:13:21,401 --> 00:13:24,318
米奇尔 帮帮忙啊
Um- Mitchell, little help?

344
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,260
不用 你说的挺好的
No. You are doing great.

345
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:29,260
看见了吧 所以说家事要忍着
See, this is exactly why we sweep things under the rug-

346
